# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for protected paths.
#
# This file only enforces anything once branch protection has
# "Require review from Code Owners" turned on for the target branch
# (Settings -> Branches -> branch protection rule). Until that box is
# checked, this file is documentation, not a gate.
#
# When more collaborators are added, extend the owner list on the
# lines below (space-separated @handles) rather than removing the
# existing owner — the point is a required reviewer other than the
# PR's author, not a single point of failure.

# Default owner for anything not matched by a more specific rule below.
*                            @danofairanks

# Published research output — the material this repo exists to
# publish. Nothing here merges without review, regardless of author.
/papers/published/          @danofairanks

# Case studies name real organizations, products, and incidents —
# the highest accuracy/defamation-risk content in the repo.
/case_studies/               @danofairanks

# Protocols define the methodology everything else is measured
# against; a silent change here invalidates prior results.
/protocols/                  @danofairanks

# Repo-level governance and configuration.
/README.md                   @danofairanks
/LICENSE                     @danofairanks
/.github/                    @danofairanks
